---
import Layout from '../layouts/Layout.astro';
import LegalLayout from '../layouts/LegalLayout.astro';

const toc = [
  { id: 'how-we-calculate', label: 'How We Calculate Results' },
  { id: 'assumptions', label: 'Assumptions' },
  { id: 'country-specific', label: 'Country-Specific Considerations' },
  { id: 'data-sources', label: 'Data and Reference Sources' },
  { id: 'accuracy', label: 'Accuracy and Limitations' },
  { id: 'review-updates', label: 'Review and Updates' },
  { id: 'disclaimer', label: 'Educational Disclaimer' },
];
---

<Layout
  title="Financial Calculator Methodology | CalcVantage"
  description="Learn how CalcVantage financial calculators work, including calculation methods, assumptions, country-specific considerations, data sources, and limitations."
  canonical="https://www.calcvantage.com/methodology"
>
  <LegalLayout
    eyebrow="Methodology"
    title="CalcVantage Calculation Methodology"
    lead="An overview of the methods, assumptions, and considerations behind every CalcVantage calculator."
    lastUpdated="August 2026"
    toc={toc}
  >
    <section class="doc-section" id="how-we-calculate">
      <h2 class="doc-section-title">How We Calculate Results</h2>
      <p class="doc-section-copy">
        CalcVantage uses standard mathematical and financial formulas appropriate to each
        calculator. The mortgage calculator applies the standard amortization formula to
        determine monthly payments, interest allocation, and remaining balance over time. The
        retirement calculator projects future savings growth using compound interest and
        contribution models. The net worth calculator computes the difference between total
        assets and total liabilities.
      </p>
      <p class="doc-section-copy">
        Each calculator is designed to be transparent. Inputs are clearly labelled, results
        include explanatory context, and the assumptions behind every number are made visible
        rather than hidden.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section" id="assumptions">
      <h2 class="doc-section-title">Assumptions</h2>
      <p class="doc-section-copy">
        Calculators may rely on assumptions that affect the results you see. These can include
        interest rates, payment frequency, inflation rates, expected investment returns,
        withdrawal rates, tax treatment, or other user-provided inputs depending on the
        calculator.
      </p>
      <p class="doc-section-copy">
        Where a calculator uses an assumption, the default value is shown and can typically be
        adjusted by the user. Assumptions are clearly indicated so you can understand what
        factors influence each result and make changes that reflect your own situation.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section" id="country-specific">
      <h2 class="doc-section-title">Country-Specific Considerations</h2>
      <p class="doc-section-copy">
        Some calculators support different rules or conventions for the United States, Canada,
        and Australia. These may include compounding frequency differences, mortgage insurance
        requirements, stamp duty calculations, or other country-specific conventions that
        affect how results are computed.
      </p>
      <p class="doc-section-copy">
        When you select a country in a calculator, the relevant rules and conventions are
        applied automatically. The calculator will indicate which country-specific factors are
        being used so you can verify the assumptions match your expectations.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section" id="data-sources">
      <h2 class="doc-section-title">Data and Reference Sources</h2>
      <p class="doc-section-copy">
        Where external rules or standards are relevant, CalcVantage may reference authoritative
        public sources and official government information. These references help ensure that
        calculations align with established financial conventions and regulatory frameworks.
      </p>
      <p class="doc-section-copy">
        CalcVantage does not fabricate data sources. If a calculator references a rule or
        standard, it is based on publicly available information relevant to the calculation
        being performed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section" id="accuracy">
      <h2 class="doc-section-title">Accuracy and Limitations</h2>
      <p class="doc-section-copy">
        All results are estimates based on user inputs and the assumptions described on this
        page. They should not be considered guaranteed financial outcomes. Actual results may
        differ based on factors not captured by any calculator, including but not limited to
        market fluctuations, fee structures, regulatory changes, and individual circumstances.
      </p>
      <p class="doc-section-copy">
        CalcVantage calculators are designed to help you explore scenarios and build
        understanding. They are not a substitute for professional financial analysis or
        personalized advice from a qualified advisor.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section" id="review-updates">
      <h2 class="doc-section-title">Review and Updates</h2>
      <p class="doc-section-copy">
        Calculation methodologies and relevant assumptions are periodically reviewed and
        updated when necessary. Updates may reflect changes in financial conventions, improved
        calculation methods, or feedback from users.
      </p>
      <p class="doc-section-copy">
        When significant changes are made, the last-updated date on this page is revised so
        you can see when the methodology was most recently reviewed.
      </p>
    </section>

    <section class="doc-section" id="disclaimer">
      <h2 class="doc-section-title">Educational Disclaimer</h2>
      <p class="doc-section-copy">
        CalcVantage provides educational calculation tools and does not provide personalized
        financial, investment, tax, legal, mortgage, or retirement advice. The information and
        calculations provided by CalcVantage are for general informational and educational
        purposes only.
      </p>
      <div class="doc-note doc-note-warning">
        <p>
          <strong>Not financial advice.</strong> Nothing on this site should be interpreted as
          personalized financial advice. Consult a qualified financial professional before
          making decisions based on the results of any calculator.
        </p>
      </div>
    </section>
  </LegalLayout>
</Layout>
